    code: { lang: "python", title: "pathlib_lesson.py — complete, runnable (Python 3.10+)", code: "import os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Build a tiny practice tree first, so the walk is identical anywhere.\nroot = Path(\"lab_tree\")\n(root / \"logs\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n(root / \"notes.txt\").write_text(\"scope: my lab only\\n\")\n(root / \"logs\" / \"auth.log\").write_text(\"Failed password for nadia\\n\")\n(root / \"logs\" / \"app.log\").write_text(\"started ok\\n\")\n\n# pathlib: paths are objects - join with /, ask questions directly.\nprint(\"auth.log exists?\", (root / \"logs\" / \"auth.log\").exists())\nprint(\"Suffix:\", (root / \"notes.txt\").suffix, \"| Name:\", (root / \"notes.txt\").name)\n\n# rglob walks the whole tree; sort for a stable listing.\nfor p in sorted(root.rglob(\"*\")):\n    kind = \"dir \" if p.is_dir() else \"file\"\n    print(f\"{kind} {p.as_posix()}\")\n\n# os and sys: the environment your tool runs in.\nprint(\"HOME set?\", \"HOME\" in os.environ or \"USERPROFILE\" in os.environ)\nprint(\"Env default:\", os.environ.get(\"CYBERLAB_MODE\", \"not set - using default\"))\nprint(\"Python major version:\", sys.version_info.major)\nprint(\"Command-line words arrive as a list in sys.argv - argparse tames them\")", output: "auth.log exists? True\nSuffix: .txt | Name: notes.txt\ndir  lab_tree/logs\nfile lab_tree/logs/app.log\nfile lab_tree/logs/auth.log\nfile lab_tree/notes.txt\nHOME set? True\nEnv default: not set - using default\nPython major version: 3\nCommand-line words arrive as a list in sys.argv - argparse tames them", lines: ["The tree is built by the program itself (mkdir + write_text), so the walk below has a known, identical answer on any machine.", "(root / 'logs' / 'auth.log') joined three pieces with / — no separator strings, no platform ifs.", "sorted() tamed rglob's filesystem order into a report order: directories and files interleaved by name.", "os.environ.get with a default printed the fallback text — the variable is unset, and the program degraded instead of crashing."] },
    mistakes: ["Gluing paths as strings with '/' or '\\' — breaks across platforms and on trailing separators; Path joins correctly.", "Reading os.environ['SECRET'] with brackets and crashing on machines where it is unset — .get with a default, and a clear error when a REQUIRED secret is missing.", "Assuming rglob order is sorted — it is filesystem order until you sort it."],
    security: "Environment variables are where tools keep tokens and target configuration — read them with defaults, never print them into logs, and never hard-code secrets in source (Level 15's secrets lesson builds on exactly this). Path discipline prevents the classic 'walked the wrong tree' evidence error.",
    pc: ["Run pathlib_lesson.py, then point rglob at a real folder of your own (your Documents) printing only .txt files, sorted.", "Set CYBERLAB_MODE=lab in your terminal (set on Windows, export on Linux) and re-run — watch the Env line change."],
    android: ["Android: interpreter apps sandbox their files; paths exist inside the app's workspace — practise the same code there with its own tree."],
    lab: "Guided lab: in the Playground, build a two-folder practice tree, then print only the .log files in it, sorted, with their sizes via p.stat().st_size.",
